caret) starts on the grid the whole screen's blur uses. Dual Kawase halves
the picture once per iteration; aligned only to `degrade`, the region was
halved on another grid and blurred slightly differently -- a faint square
around the pointer, a terminal flickering where its cursor blinks (Vini).

